  "description": "<p>The idea is to add two headers to all API responses to help call attention to the importance of user registration. </p>\n\n<p>USER-REGISTRATION: “</p>\n{user registration call to action here including link}\n<p>“</p>\n\n<p>{{Link: &lt;</p>\n{user registration link}\n<p>&gt;; rel=\"user-regisration”}}</p>\n\n<p>Text to be determined by <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=611688a84f9756006acc770b\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"611688a84f9756006acc770b\" data-account-id=\"611688a84f9756006acc770b\" accountid=\"611688a84f9756006acc770b\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Arran Griffith</a> </p>\n\n<p>If would be nice to add a system property such as fcrepo.user-registration-header.enabled (default to true) so that users can turn these messages off.</p>",
